py3.14t and 'still runs' on the GIL py3.14 leg. Pytest prints skip reasons only with -rs/-ra, and per-test PASSED lines only with -v or a junit report. 'no longer fails' alone cannot tell skipped-with-the-right-reason apart from skipped-for-another-reason or deselected. Likewise, it cannot tell ran-and-passed on py3.14 apart from silently skipped.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fb42fa0f0c7a6b42d","impact":0.44,"is_primary":null,"location":"Testing — 'Free-threaded build' bullet; Acceptance Criteria item 2","norm_id":"n1462be469f17650d","priority":0.2514,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["The CI pytest invocation lacks -rs, so the reason never appears in the log and the AC is signed off on 'job didn't fail'.","The new skipif condition accidentally evaluates truthy on GIL 3.14 as well. Both legs go green, and nothing shows the test stopped running on py3.14."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"In Testing, add: 'In the py3.14t job log, confirm a line matching `SKIPPED .*test_mcp_idle_heap_release.py.*mimalloc` (run with -rs, or inspect the junit report). In the py3.14 job, confirm `test_finished_background_job_does_not_keep_its_memory PASSED` (or no <skipped> element for it in junit).'","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5714,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"na","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Before submitting to Gerrit, run the test file once on a free-threaded 3.14t interpreter with -rs and record the SKIPPED line with the mimalloc reason. Alternatively, state why only the post-merge check is possible.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5a","T5b","T5e","T7"],"criteria":["E6","F1"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.6,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'after merge, dispatch `gh workflow run test.yml --ref main`'","'`sweep (py3.14t)` is an experimental, nonblocking leg'","'`make verify` green in the worktree' (runs on the worktree's default GIL interpreter)"],"finding":"The only check on the free-threaded path runs post-merge, on a leg the plan calls nonblocking. So the Gerrit Verified +1 / `make verify` gate never runs the new skip condition on a free-threaded interpreter. A wrong condition, for example one that evaluates falsy on 3.14t, would merge and leave main's py3.14t sweep red. The plan names no pre-merge exercise of the change on 3.14t.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fae78c099e4d352b8","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Testing; Acceptance Criteria items 2-3","norm_id":"n160f9182da5b3678","priority":0.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["`sysconfig.get_config_var(\"Py_GIL_DISABLED\")` returns a value the condition doesn't treat as truthy. The change merges green and the sweep still fails, so a follow-up change is needed."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add a Testing bullet: 'Pre-merge: `uv run --python 3.14t pytest tests/unit/test_mcp_idle_heap_release.py -rs` shows the memory test SKIPPED with the mimalloc reason; on the default GIL interpreter the same command shows it PASSED (Linux).'","tier":"LLM","validity":0.625,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"na","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Add an AC stating that `release_freed_heap`'s docstring notes that on free-threaded builds Python objects are allocated by mimalloc, which `malloc_trim` does not release.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5a","T5b","T5e","T7"],"criteria":["E1"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.7143,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Scope: '`src/rebar/_mcp_health.py` — docstring sentence on `release_freed_heap` only.'","Approach: 'Add one sentence to `release_freed_heap`'s docstring stating that on free-threaded builds Python objects live in mimalloc, which `malloc_trim` does not govern.'","No AC references the docstring."],"finding":"The docstring change to `release_freed_heap` in `src/rebar/_mcp_health.py` is a listed deliverable with no covering acceptance criterion. Every AC concerns the test skip, root cause, or verify/Gerrit, so the docstring sentence could be omitted with all ACs still checked.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f6aa543835da64393","impact":0.55,"is_primary":null,"location":"Scope — `src/rebar/_mcp_health.py` bullet; Acceptance Criteria","norm_id":"nb1ab116b051d1496","priority":0.2357,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["The executor lands the test skip only; review passes against the ACs, and the production function keeps no record of its free-threaded limitation."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add AC: '- [ ] `release_freed_heap` docstring in src/rebar/_mcp_health.py states that on free-threaded (Py_GIL_DISABLED) builds Python objects live in mimalloc, which malloc_trim does not release.'","tier":"LLM","validity":0.4286,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"na","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"underspecified_certification","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Recast AC 1 as a durable artifact: the commit message (or a ticket comment) records the 13/13 py3.14t failure evidence and the mimalloc root cause, and the skip reason references mimalloc.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5a","T5b","T5e","T7"],"criteria":["F1"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.6,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'- [ ] Root cause identified with evidence (deterministic on free-threaded builds vs intermittent).'","Context already contains the evidence (13/13 runs, job 135106845268 figures, the allocator explanation)."],"finding":"AC 1, 'Root cause identified with evidence', is a one-time transition that the plan's own Context section already satisfies. It is not a durable end-state of the change, and it names no artifact where the evidence must persist (commit message, skip reason, ticket comment).","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f0ebe20d790a4188c","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria item 1","norm_id":"n18d9d09e4d14299a","priority":0.0,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["The checkbox is ticked from the plan text alone, and the diagnosis never reaches the commit or code, so a later reader of the skip has no trail."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Replace AC 1 with: '- [ ] The commit message records the root cause (free-threaded PyObject_Malloc → mimalloc, not released by malloc_trim) and the evidence (13/13 deterministic py3.14t failures, ~272 MiB retained, py3.14 passing on the same runner).'","tier":"LLM","validity":0.2857,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"na","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Before dispatching, confirm GitHub main contains the merged commit (wait for replication), state the gh auth precondition, and check the run's headSha equals the merged SHA when judging AC 2.","cohort":["T3"],"criteria":["T3"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.9,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan quote: \"after merge, dispatch `gh workflow run test.yml --ref main`\"","Partially-verified: .github/workflows/mirror-guard.yml:3-5 — \"Check Gerrit-to-GitHub main replication ... so ordinary propagation lag does not alert\"","Absence: no step confirms that GitHub main contains the merged change before dispatching, and no step checks that the run's headSha matches it","Absence: no gh auth precondition (an authenticated gh with actions write on the GitHub repo) is stated"],"finding":"The post-merge verification dispatches `gh workflow run test.yml --ref main` right after the merge. GitHub main is an asynchronously replicated mirror of Gerrit with known propagation lag, so the dispatched run may check out the pre-merge SHA. That would fail the test again, or falsely appear to confirm the fix. The plan also doesn't state the gh authentication/permission needed to dispatch a workflow.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f4505e17fea233ba0","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Testing — 'after merge, dispatch `gh workflow run test.yml --ref main`'; AC 2 'On the post-merge `sweep (py3.14t)` job'","norm_id":"n93fb1e66a68823c4","priority":0.0,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["The dispatch fires before replication finishes: sweep (py3.14t) runs the old test, fails at ~272 MiB, and the AC appears unmet.","The run is attributed to the fix without checking its headSha against the merged commit."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"In Testing, add: 'Wait until `git ls-remote https://github.com/<repo> main` (or mirror-guard) shows the merged SHA, then run `gh workflow run test.yml --ref main` with an authenticated gh (actions:write). Confirm the sweep (py3.14t) run's headSha (`gh run view <id> --json headSha`) equals the merged commit before recording the skip.'","tier":"LLM","validity":0.25,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"insufficient","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}}],"impact_model_version":"plan-v5","material_fingerprint":"48c5c027f8d4ca40","material_parts":{"children":["647ea2107ca5072f",0],"description":["15878c92bf08993f",3422],"description_boxes":["0aad7da77d2ed59c",0],"file_impact":["dc0c9fdd135ab92b",2],"ticket_id":["c37aa87ae62ea48d",19]},"metrics":{"cache_read_tokens":156436,"cache_write_tokens":83104,"claim_path":"no-llm/no-network (structural; the fast claim check is a local HMAC verify)","det_ms":6207.0,"input_tokens":262988,"llm_calls":31,"llm_ms":81896.1,"output_tokens":24342,"precheck":{"cited_anchor_warning":false},"total_ms":97674.9,"verify_requests":1},"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-5-5","provider_provenance":{"candidates":["bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-5-5","anthropic:claude-sonnet-5-5"],"capabilities":{"native_structured_output